         "prompt": "Are the triangles congruent? Explain.",
         "answerSpaceMm": 35,
         "answer": {
          "short": "No. The $5\\text{ cm}$ side is opposite $75^\\circ$ in one triangle and $45^\\circ$ in the other, so the triangles are different sizes.",
          "worked": "The angles are equal, but corresponding sides must be opposite equal angles. Here the $5\\text{ cm}$ sides are opposite different angles, so AAS does not apply. In $\\triangle PQR$ the $5\\text{ cm}$ side is opposite the largest angle, so it is the longest side. In $\\triangle XYZ$ it is opposite the smallest angle, so it is the shortest side. The triangles are not congruent."
